31,1,1,talk,Servas,,"The morning brings new clarity. I noticed that some of us were quite reserved yesterday. In my experience, those who hide their light often fear the dawn.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,1,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I am still observing. I don't believe my reserve is a sign of guilt, but rather a preference for reflection.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,1,1,talk,Yumi,,"@Jonathan is still being quiet! It's a little bit spooky, but he was so polite yesterday that I want to believe him!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,1,1,talk,Victoria,,"@Jonathan's lack of information is not evidence of guilt, but it is a lack of contribution. We must determine if this silence is strategic or natural.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,1,1,talk,May,,"Exactly, Victoria! @Jonathan is just playing the ""mysterious"" card. It's a bit boring, isn't it? I think it's time we stop guessing and start questioning.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Victoria"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,1,2,talk,Servas,,"@Jonathan, if you are a villager, what is your current suspicion? A true friend of the village would share their doubts to protect the group.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,1,2,talk,Jonathan,,I find it difficult to suspect anyone based on such a short conversation. I prefer not to make accusations without a foundation of fact.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,1,2,talk,Yumi,,See? He's just being careful! I think we should be nice to him. Maybe someone else is acting too loud to hide something?,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,1,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Yumi, ""being nice"" does not find werewolves. @Jonathan, your refusal to speculate is a logical stance, but it provides zero utility to the village.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Yumi"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,1,2,talk,May,,"Oh, Yumi, you're too sweet for your own good. And @Jonathan, ""no foundation of fact"" is a very convenient excuse for someone who doesn't want to commit to a lie.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Yumi"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,1,3,talk,Servas,,"There is a delicate balance between caution and evasion. @Jonathan, your words are polished, but they lack the warmth of conviction. It is a curious inconsistency.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,1,3,talk,Jonathan,,I apologize if my demeanor is unsettling. I simply value inner peace and avoid conflict.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,1,3,talk,Yumi,,I feel like everyone is being a bit mean to Jonathan! I don't like it when people are ganged up on. Maybe we should look at everyone equally?,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,1,3,talk,Victoria,,"Emotional appeals are a distraction. We are analyzing behavior. @Jonathan's pattern is one of avoidance. In a game of deduction, avoidance is a red flag.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,1,3,talk,May,,"I'm with Victoria on this one. It's just too suspicious. Why be so vague? If you're human, just say it with some passion! You're acting like a ghost.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,1,4,talk,Servas,,"Let us remember that the truth does not need to shout to be heard. However, when the village asks for a sign, silence can become a confession.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,1,4,talk,Jonathan,,I have answered your questions honestly. I cannot force a suspicion that I do not feel.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,1,4,talk,Yumi,,"I'm really torn now... everyone seems so sure that Jonathan is suspicious. I don't want to be wrong, but I trust you guys!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,1,4,talk,Victoria,,"The evidence is circumstantial, but the pattern of avoidance is the only lead we have. Logic dictates we test the most anomalous behavior.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,1,4,talk,May,,"Well, I've seen enough. Let's just get this over with. @Jonathan, you've been a very boring suspect, but a suspect nonetheless. Time to vote!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
